@startuml azure-entra-auth-with-roles
!theme plain
title Azure Entra ID Authentication with Role Synchronization

actor User
participant "Browser" as Browser
participant "Laravel App\n(showcase)" as App
participant "Azure Entra\nOAuth2" as Azure
participant "Microsoft Graph\nAPI" as Graph
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

User -> Browser: 1. Clicca "Sign in with Microsoft"
Browser -> App: 2. GET /auth/azure
App -> Azure: 3. Redirect to Azure login\n(client_id, redirect_uri, scope)
Azure -> Browser: 4. Azure login screen
User -> Azure: 5. Inserisce credenziali
Azure -> Browser: 6. Authorization code
Browser -> App: 7. GET /auth/azure/callback?code=CODE
App -> Azure: 8. POST /token\n(code, client_id, client_secret)
Azure -> App: 9. access_token, id_token, refresh_token
App -> App: 10. Socialite resolves user profile
App -> App: 11. updateOrCreate User in DB
DB -> DB: 12. User record created/updated\n(azure_id, token, refresh_token)
App -> App: 13. Start role sync
App -> Graph: 14. GET /me/memberOf\n(authorization: Bearer access_token)
Graph -> App: 15. Group memberships\n[{id, displayName, ...}]
App -> App: 16. Upsert roles by group
DB -> DB: 17. Sync roles table\n(azure_group_id, name, permissions)
App -> App: 18. Sync user_roles
DB -> DB: 19. Insert/Delete user_roles\n(user_id, role_id)
App -> Browser: 20. Set session cookie
App -> Browser: 21. Redirect to /
Browser -> App: 22. GET /
App -> Browser: 23. Inertia page\n(auth + user + roles + permissions)
Browser -> User: 24. Dashboard loaded

== Runtime authorization refresh ==
Browser -> App: 25. Request authenticated route
App -> App: 26. roles.synced middleware checks TTL
alt TTL expired
  App -> Graph: 27. GET /me/memberOf
  Graph -> App: 28. Updated memberships
  App -> DB: 29. Resync roles and user_roles
end

alt Roles removed and invalidation enabled
  App -> Graph: 30. POST /me/revokeSignInSessions (optional)
  Graph -> App: 31. 2xx (revokes refresh/session tokens)
  App -> Browser: 32. Local logout + session invalidation
  App -> Browser: 33. Redirect to /login
end

note over App
  **Service Layer**
  - RoleManagementService
    - syncUserRoles(user, access_token)
    - getUserGroupsFromGraph(access_token)
    - syncRolesInDatabase(groups)
    - assignRolesToUser(user, roleIds)
    - revokeCurrentUserSignInSessions(access_token) [optional]
end note

note over Graph
  **Delegated scopes**
  - User.Read
  - GroupMember.Read.All (admin consent required)
  - User.RevokeSessions.All (optional, admin consent required)
end note

note over Azure,Graph
  Microsoft-side revocation mainly invalidates refresh/session tokens.
  Existing access tokens can remain valid until expiry or CAE enforcement.
  Group membership changes are not guaranteed to invalidate tokens immediately.
end note

note over DB
  **Schema**
  roles:
  - id, name, azure_group_id,
    permissions (JSON), created_at

  user_roles:
  - user_id, role_id, created_at
end note
@enduml
